//RS /// the columns — never in the layout, the row bookkeeping, the bounds policy, or
//RS /// the read (I9).
//RS ///
//RS /// `C` is the tier's cell: `JetVal` for Cranelift, `CtValue` for the ambient,
//RS /// and a generated per-struct cell enum for AOT. Holding the cell abstract is
//RS /// exactly what the ratified tradeoff bought — a tagged cell costs a little
//RS /// speed against a layout tuned per struct, and a tuned column can be added
//RS /// later behind this same read without moving the policy back into an engine.
